task.prompt_template:
Assess this single system-state snapshot. Use only these observations; do not recommend or trigger actions. A flow row's working/done value is UI state, not proof that its task is healthy or complete. Queue addresses identify flows; queue contents are intentionally withheld. Host load averages measure runnable work over time, not current CPU utilization; do not infer CPU utilization from them. Energy percentages and pace labels are cached weekly Energy Nexus readings, not a policy verdict; their observation time and age are shown. Use Unknown for a judgment when the snapshot lacks relevant evidence or a configured baseline/threshold. Set flow_load to exactly one of TooMany, Appropriate, TooFew, or Unknown. Set energy_use to exactly one of TooHigh, Appropriate, TooLow, or Unknown. Return exactly one JSON object: either {"kind":"Answered","answer":{"flow_load":"one enum value","energy_use":"one enum value","reason":"nonempty evidence-based explanation"}} or {"kind":"Refused","reason":"nonempty explanation"}. Do not include markdown or other text.

